# Pages and breaks: After: page sends what follows a box to a new page.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Pages and breaks · Break after
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 15mm
	Page overlay:
		Offset: auto 0 -24 0
		Text: Page {page} of {pages}
			Typography:
				Align: right
	Section:
		Text: Pages and breaks
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Break after
		Paragraph: With `After: page`, what follows the box starts on a new page. The box itself stays where it is. A forced break after the last box of a section does nothing, so it never adds a blank page.
			Style: intro
		Block:
			Style: marked
			Break:
				After: page
			Text: Break: After: page
				Style: label
			Paragraph: This block ends page 1. The next one goes to page 2.
		Block:
			Style: marked
			Text: Break: (none)
				Style: label
			Paragraph: This block starts page 2 because the one before it asked for the break.
